claim.claim-text:
a tank (10) for receiving a photo-curing liquid material;
at least one extraction plate (15) provided with means of movement (16) with alternating rectilinear motion, in a direction perpendicular to a bottom (11) of said tank (10);
a first source (12) of a photo-curing radiation of a first predetermined wavelength and a first polarization, the first source (12) being of the DLP type;
a second source (13) of a photo-curing radiation of a predetermined second wavelength and a second polarization orthogonal to the first polarization, the second source being of the laser type; and
laser deflection means and/or a polarizing beam combiner (19), particularly a polarisation coupling optic (19), which is particularly assigned to the first source (12) and/or to the second source (13).

a) lowering the extraction plate (15) to a position where the last cured layer, or in its absence the lower surface of the extraction plate (15), is at the distance of a layer to be formed with respect to the bottom (11) of the tank (10);
b) proceeding with the irradiation and the generation of one cured layer of the object to be printed;
c) lifting the extraction plate (15), with progressive detachment of the bottom (11) of the tank (10) from the cured layer;
then iteratively repeating the steps a)-c) until completion of the object to be formed.
